WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.850
Lab 1 runs on a laptop with no tenant.

2
00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.900
First, run Learn's
tutorial against the fake.

3
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.985
Eleven tests pass, and the
third one shows the trap:

4
00:00:08.985 --> 00:00:13.650
send the tutorial's request twice, and
you get two reviews with the same name.

5
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.086
Next, list each task's permissions:

6
00:00:16.086 --> 00:00:20.262
reads for planning and evidence,
writes only for the apply.

7
00:00:20.262 --> 00:00:21.512
Then the dry run.

8
00:00:21.512 --> 00:00:25.434
It finds one series to create,
two to update, one to replace,

9
00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:29.774
three already right, and one
somebody made by hand in the portal.

10
00:00:29.774 --> 00:00:30.950
Nothing is sent.

11
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:35.780
Only two writes would go out, because the
Azure update needs the preview switch.
